{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"agent_message","text":"# Implementation Notes\n\n## Decisions Made\n- Added hourly light, chemistry, dissolved-oxygen, and event systems in `tank_core` and wired them into `Engine::step_one_hour` after temperature, before time advances.\n- Stored runtime pH on `state.water.ph` and moved NH3 speciation to a shared `compute_nh3_mg_l` helper used by both event emission and `TankSnapshot`.\n- Added per-kind daily event dedup with `state.last_event_day`, plus invariant handling for non-negative DO and clamped pH.\n- Extended `ProcessParams` and the process preset pipeline in `tank_data`/`tank_scenarios` so scenario-loaded states get active Loop 3 chemistry/DO coefficients.\n- Kept `ProcessParams::default()` neutral for DIC drift while leaving the preset pack active, so legacy no-op water-change behavior still passes without weakening existing tests.\n\n## Spec Deviations\n- `ProcessParams::default()` uses `0.0` for the new DIC respiration/photosynthesis rates, while the shipped process preset enables them. This preserves existing constructor-based regression behavior; scenario/preset-driven simulations still exercise the new pH drift model.\n- Step 11 was implemented as part of the new chemistry and dissolved-oxygen systems rather than as a separate standalone hourly plant-effects module.\n\n## Testing\n- Added new regression tests in `crates/tank_core/tests/dissolved_oxygen.rs`, `crates/tank_core/tests/chemistry.rs`, and `crates/tank_core/tests/events.rs` for night DO dips, aeration recovery, reaeration convergence, pH drift, NH3 speciation, threshold events, and daily dedup.\n- Verified the full workspace with:\n  - `nix shell nixpkgs#cargo nixpkgs#rustc nixpkgs#gcc -c cargo test`\n- Result: full workspace test suite passed, including `save_load_resume`, determinism, existing water-change/thermal tests, and the new Loop 3 coverage.\n\n---"}}
